{"body":"## Current friction\n\nAttaching metadata to a newly added artifact takes at least two commands today. After `rad-artifact add ...` succeeds, the user has to capture the CID printed to stderr and issue one `rad-artifact metadata set --revision <rev> --cid <cid> KEY VALUE` per entry. For scripted releases that publish a binary with build-env, version, reproducibility, or SBOM metadata, that's brittle (parse stderr or recompute the CID) and several round-trips per artifact.\n\n## What's missing\n\n`rad-artifact add` should accept metadata pairs in the same invocation, so a release can be published with its full metadata in one shot.\n\n## Proposed shape\n\nTwo new flags on `add`, mirroring the existing `metadata set` semantics:\n\n- `--meta KEY=VALUE` (repeatable) — stores the value as a JSON string, like `metadata set` without `--json`.\n- `--meta-json` (boolean) — when set, every `--meta` value in the same invocation is parsed as JSON instead, like `metadata set --json`. All-or-nothing per call.\n\nExamples:\n\n```\nrad-artifact add ./my-binary --revision v1.0 --name \"my-binary v1.0\" \\\n  --meta build-env=\"nix --pure\" --meta version=1.0\n\nrad-artifact add ./my-binary --revision v1.0 --name \"my-binary v1.0\" --meta-json \\\n  --meta reproducible=true --meta 'sbom={\"format\":\"cyclonedx\",\"url\":\"...\"}'\n```\n\nAll pairs should be validated (existing key rules + 8 KiB value cap) before the artifact is committed, so a bad pair can't leave an artifact registered without its intended metadata.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `rad-artifact add` accepts a repeatable `--meta KEY=VALUE` flag.\n- [ ] `--meta-json` switches all `--meta` values in the same invocation to JSON-parsed.\n- [ ] All entries are validated before the artifact is added; invalid input results in zero side effects.\n- [ ] Existing `add` behavior is unchanged when no `--meta` flags are passed.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG entry under \"Unreleased\".\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Adding a multi-entry mode to `metadata set` (could come later for symmetry).\n- Atomic add-plus-metadata in a single COB transaction — pre-validation already prevents partial-state surprises.","type":"comment"}